# List-Dashboard-First Feature Development

For configurable list/detail/form features, use `@nabarun-ngo/list-dashboard-core`
and `@nabarun-ngo/list-dashboard-angular`. Do not import or recreate Experience
Framework packages (`@nabarun-ngo/experience-*` were removed).

## Reference implementation

Signed-off pilot to copy: `apps/internal-app/src/app/feature/finance/donation/`  
Pilot docs: `apps/internal-app/docs/README.md`

## Mandatory consumer structure

Exactly four folders — no others:

```text
feature/<domain>/<entity>/
├── config/    # <entity>.config.ts (only public factory) + forms/rules/view
├── data/      # port, providers, api/demo, DTO→domain mapper
├── domain/    # pure models
└── page/      # thin route host binding na-list-dashboard
```

Forbidden folders: `experience/`, `forms/`, `preparation/`, `operations/`,
`mappers/`, `services/`, `application/`, `presentation/`, `pages/`.

## Boundaries

- Page binds `[config]` to `<na-list-dashboard>` only.
- Domain I/O, mapping, preparation, actions, and operations live in `config/`.
- `data/` maps API DTOs → domain only — never `ListRowItem`.
- UI row/detail shaping lives in `config/<entity>.view.ts`.
- Nested collections use `type: 'item_list'` sections — never forRoot widgets.
- `forRoot` registers only DocumentList + FileUpload.
- Shared packages must never branch on an entity name or import feature code.
- Create deep links must run `createOpen` preparation before opening the sheet.
- Condition-hidden field values must not be submitted.

## Forbidden legacy

Do not create entity dashboard/list/detail adapter classes, direct
`FilteredListDashboardController` wiring in pages, or custom sheets that
duplicate the generic list-dashboard host.
